Day 21 Notes – React Router

1.Install
npm install react-router-dom

2.Wrap the App (in main.jsx)
import { BrowserRouter } from "react-router-dom";
<BrowserRouter><App /></BrowserRouter>

3.Create Pages
function Home() {
return Home Page;
}
export default Home;

4.Navigation + Routes (in App.jsx)
import { Routes, Route, Link } from "react-router-dom";

  <link to="/">Home
  <link to="/about">About
  <link to="/todo">Todo

<Routes>
<Route path="/" element={<Home />} />
<Route path="/about" element={<About />} />
<Route path="/todo" element={<div>Todo Page</div>} />
</Routes>

Key Points:
-Link → used for navigation (like  tag)
-Routes → contains all pages
-Route → defines one page
-path="/" → home page
-element={} → which component to show
